# --- generated / regenerable ---------------------------------------------
# _raw_ids.json is 17 MB of intermediate data produced by
# _probe/semantic/extract_ids.py from the shipped .dat in ~5 s.  It is an input
# to build_semantic.py, never a source: committing it would make every clone
# carry a copy of the game's data.
_probe/semantic/_raw_ids.json
_probe/semantic/_unresolved_ids.json
_probe/semantic/_tech_diag.json
_probe/schema/AGE3NamesV0007.json
_probe/schema/age_label_tables_raw.json

# The AGE source tree is extracted from the game's own
# Tools_Builds/docs/Source.7z.  It is third-party source under GPLv3/LGPLv3,
# it is 2.4 MB of C++, and it is reproducible from the installed game:
#   tar -xf "<game>/Tools_Builds/docs/Source.7z" -C _probe/source
# Keeping it out of the repo keeps the licence question out of the repo too.
_probe/source/
aoe2docs/

# --- python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc

# --- outputs --------------------------------------------------------------
_probe/out_*/
_probe/out_*.txt
发布包/
_shots/
*.zip
*.7z

# --- scratch --------------------------------------------------------------
_probe/tmp_*.py
_probe/_newlog.md

# --- team audit artifacts --------------------------------------------------
# Each auditor teammate copies its own aoe2mod tree and dozens of 11.4 MB .dat
# scratch copies; keep only their REPORT.md, never the scratch/mutation forests.
_probe/team/*/scratch/
_probe/team/*/mutations/
_probe/team/*/__pycache__/

# The artifact emitter's scratch: 11.4 MB of .dat per run, regenerable by
# _probe/datparse/emit_mod.py (which verify_artifact.py then checks).
_probe/datparse/out_modtest/

# _probe/verify_agevariant_artifact.py's scratch mod (11.9 MB .dat).  Note the
# pattern above (_probe/out_*/) does NOT cover a directory named just out.
_probe/out/

# _probe/test_sld_encode.py writes a repainted .sld here (703 KB, regenerable).
_probe/_sld_out/
